      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nTNpZ",
      "text": "<math><mi>N</mi><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> will have configuration <math><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.93</mn><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math><br /><br />or, <math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> as <math><msqrt><mn>35</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>5.93</mn></math><br /><br />If has <math><mn>5</mn></math> unpaired electron which are not getting paired up. This implies that the ligand paired up, and the ligand is a weak field ligand. Among the given options, weak ligand is <math><mi>N</mi><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
